# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# Data / DB — never commit the DB or captured data (it lives on disk / archive)
# NOTE: `data/*`, not `data/` — git does not descend into an excluded DIRECTORY, so a `!` exception
# cannot re-include anything under it. With `data/` the un-ignore below silently does nothing.
data/*
# ★2026-08-04 EXCEPTION (operator: "track exit_overrides.json in git").
# This file decides EVERY exit on the live desk (per-gate a_r/b plus the quiet-tape clip) and was
# untracked, so there was no record of what the desk was actually running on any given day. Concrete
# cost, found the same day: the stop-width study could not evaluate 2026-07-31→08-02 at all, because the
# live exit ladder for that window is UNRECOVERABLE — not hard to find, gone — with only two undated
# ad-hoc snapshots surviving. The trailing `*` deliberately covers those .pre-* snapshots too, so no
# future one is lost either.
!data/exit_overrides.json*
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.parquet

# Secrets / env
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Scratch / logs
scratch/
*.log
backups/
data/claim_pin.txt
data/claim_requests.txt
